🎯 Types of System Calls

Interview Favorite.

There are 6 major categories.

1️⃣ Process Control System Calls

Used for:

✅ Create Process

✅ Terminate Process

✅ Execute Program

Examples:

fork()

Creates child process.

exec()

Loads new program.

exit()

Terminates process.

wait()

Wait for child process.

Example:

Chrome opens new tab.

OS creates process/thread.

System Calls used.

2️⃣ File Management System Calls

Used for files.

Examples:

open()

Open file.

read()

Read file.

write()

Write file.

close()

Close file.

Example:

Opening:

Resume.pdf

OS internally executes:

open()
read()
close()
3️⃣ Device Management System Calls

Used for hardware devices.

Examples:

ioctl()

Control device.

read()

Read keyboard input.

write()

Write to printer.

Example:

Press keyboard key.

System call interacts with device driver.

4️⃣ Information Maintenance System Calls

Used to get system information.

Examples:

getpid()

Get Process ID.

getuid()

Get User ID.

time()

Get system time.

Example:

Task Manager showing PID.

Uses system calls.

5️⃣ Communication System Calls

Used for IPC (Inter Process Communication).

Examples:

pipe()

Create pipe.

socket()

Create network socket.

send()

Send data.

recv()

Receive data.

Example:

WhatsApp message sent.

Uses:

socket()
send()
6️⃣ Protection System Calls

Used for security.

Examples:

chmod()

Change permissions.

chown()

Change owner.

setuid()

Change user privileges.

Example:

Making file read-only.

Uses protection system calls.

